What I Learned – Days of the Week Using Switch Case in C

Today, I created a Days of the Week program using the C programming language.

Through this program, I learned:

How to use the switch statement for decision-making.
How case statements execute different blocks of code based on user input.
How the break statement stops the execution of a switch case.
How the default case handles invalid input.
How scanf() is used to get input from the user.
How to use printf() to display the corresponding day of the week.
Important Logic / Formula

Switch Case Logic

Input: day (1–7)
Case 1: Monday
Case 2: Tuesday
Case 3: Wednesday
Case 4: Thursday
Case 5: Friday
Case 6: Saturday
Case 7: Sunday
Default: Invalid day

Project Goal

To understand and practice decision-making using the switch statement in C. 
This program demonstrates how user input can be used to execute different cases and display the corresponding day of the week. 
It also helps improve my understanding of conditional control flow and basic input/output operations in C.